stream
BT /F2 16 Tf 56 762.8 Td (SMS-11 Enclosed Space Entry) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 720.7 Td (Standard Operating Procedure: Enclosed Space Entry) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 678.7 Td (Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 649.7 Td (This procedure establishes the mandatory safety protocols for all personnel entering) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 635.2 Td (enclosed spaces aboard the vessel. An enclosed space is defined as any area with limited) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 620.7 Td (means of entry or exit that is not designed for continuous human occupancy, including but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 606.2 Td (not limited to cargo holds, ballast tanks, fuel oil tanks, void spaces, and pump rooms.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 577.2 Td (The primary objective is to prevent fatalities and injuries resulting from atmospheric) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 562.7 Td (hazards, entrapment, or mechanical failure during entry. This protocol applies to all crew) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 548.2 Td (members, contractors, and visitors who may require access to such areas. No individual is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 533.7 Td (permitted to enter an enclosed space without strict adherence to the steps outlined in this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 519.2 Td (document. Violation of these procedures constitutes a serious breach of safety regulations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 504.7 Td (and will result in immediate disciplinary action.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 462.6 Td (Permit to Enter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 433.6 Td (Access to any enclosed space is strictly controlled through a formal Permit to Enter system.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 419.1 Td (The issuance of this permit is the sole responsibility of the Master, who retains ultimate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 404.6 Td (authority over all entry operations. Before a permit can be signed, the Officer in Charge) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 390.1 Td (must verify that all preparatory safety measures have been completed and validated.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 361.1 Td (The permit serves as legal authorization for entry and must be physically signed by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 346.6 Td (Master prior to any personnel crossing the threshold into the space. The validity of this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 332.1 Td (permit is strictly limited to one shift of maximum 8 hours. If the work extends beyond this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 317.6 Td (timeframe, or if the shift changes, the previous permit must be cancelled, and a new permit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 303.1 Td (must be issued following a fresh assessment of conditions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 274.1 Td (The permit document itself must clearly state the specific location being entered, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 259.6 Td (nature of the work to be performed, the names of all personnel entering, and the time of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 245.1 Td (issuance. It is imperative that the permit remains visible at the entrance of the space for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 230.6 Td (the duration of the entry. If any condition changes or if an emergency occurs, the permit is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 216.1 Td (immediately voided until a new assessment is conducted.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 174.1 Td (Atmosphere Testing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 145.1 Td (Atmospheric testing is the critical first step in ensuring the safety of entrants. Before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 130.6 Td (any ventilation begins, initial testing must be carried out to establish baseline) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 116.1 Td (conditions. The space must be ventilated for at least 30 minutes before testing to ensure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 101.6 Td (that stagnant air pockets are cleared and that fresh air has circulated throughout the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 87.1 Td (volume.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (SMS-11 Enclosed Space Entry \(fictional\) - page 1 of 3) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
