5 0 obj
<< /Length 4204 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 757.0 Td (Testing must be conducted using calibrated, multi-gas detectors capable of measuring oxygen,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 742.5 Td (combustible gases, hydrogen sulfide, and carbon monoxide simultaneously. Samples must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 728.0 Td (taken at the top, middle, and bottom of the space, as different gases have varying densities) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 713.5 Td (and may stratify. Testing should occur immediately before entry and continuously during the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 699.0 Td (operation if portable monitors are used.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 670.0 Td (The atmosphere is only considered acceptable for entry if it meets all of the following) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 655.5 Td (criteria simultaneously:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 641.0 Td (- Oxygen levels must be exactly 20.8% by volume. Levels below this indicate potential) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 626.5 Td (  asphyxiation risks, while levels above may indicate oxygen enrichment hazards.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 612.0 Td (- Hydrocarbon concentrations must remain below 1% LFL \(Lower Flammability Limit\). Any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 597.5 Td (  reading above this threshold requires immediate ventilation and re-testing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 583.0 Td (- Hydrogen sulfide \(H2S\) levels must be below 5 ppm. H2S is highly toxic and can cause) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 568.5 Td (  rapid unconsciousness even at low concentrations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 554.0 Td (- Carbon monoxide \(CO\) levels must be below 25 ppm. CO is odorless and deadly, requiring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 539.5 Td (  strict monitoring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 510.5 Td (If any parameter falls outside these acceptable limits, entry is prohibited until corrective) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 496.0 Td (action restores the atmosphere to safe levels. Ventilation must continue, and re-testing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 481.5 Td (must confirm safety before a permit can be signed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 439.4 Td (Attendant and Communication) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 410.4 Td (A dedicated attendant must remain at the entrance of the enclosed space at all times while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 395.9 Td (personnel are inside. The attendant's primary role is to monitor the entrants and maintain) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 381.4 Td (communication; they are strictly prohibited from entering the space under any circumstances) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 366.9 Td (unless authorized by a specific rescue protocol. The attendant must maintain constant visual) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 352.4 Td (or verbal contact with the entrants.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 323.4 Td (Communication checks must be performed every 10 minutes. These checks serve to confirm that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 308.9 Td (all entrants are conscious, aware of their surroundings, and in good health. If) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 294.4 Td (communication is lost for any reason, or if an entrant reports feeling unwell, all personnel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 279.9 Td (must exit the space immediately, and the permit must be suspended.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 250.9 Td (The attendant must possess a fully charged two-way radio or other reliable communication) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 236.4 Td (device compatible with the vessel's network. They must also have immediate access to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 221.9 Td (emergency alarm system. The attendant is responsible for logging the time of each) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 207.4 Td (communication check on the permit document. This log provides a critical record of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 192.9 Td (entrants' status throughout the duration of the work.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 150.9 Td (Rescue) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 121.9 Td (Preparedness for rescue operations is non-negotiable. The vessel must maintain a dedicated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 107.4 Td (enclosed space rescue team that is trained and equipped to respond to emergencies within) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 92.9 Td (these confined areas. This team must have access to appropriate breathing apparatus,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 78.4 Td (harnesses, tripods, and winches suitable for the specific geometry of each enclosed space.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (SMS-11 Enclosed Space Entry \(fictional\) - page 2 of 3) Tj ET
endstream
