BT /F1 10 Tf 56 757.0 Td (To ensure readiness, enclosed space rescue drills are held every 2 months. These drills) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 742.5 Td (simulate realistic scenarios, including unconscious entrants and equipment failure, to test) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 728.0 Td (the response time and effectiveness of the rescue team. Drills must be debriefed afterward) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 713.5 Td (to identify gaps in procedure or equipment maintenance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 684.5 Td (In the event of an emergency, the attendant must immediately raise the general alarm and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 670.0 Td (notify the bridge. The Master will initiate the vessel's Emergency Response Plan. Rescue) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 655.5 Td (operations must only proceed if the rescuers are protected from the same hazards that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 641.0 Td (endangered the entrants. Unprotected entry by rescuers is strictly forbidden due to the high) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 626.5 Td (risk of multiple fatalities.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 584.4 Td (Records) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 555.4 Td (Accurate documentation is essential for regulatory compliance and operational continuity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 540.9 Td (All completed permits to enter enclosed spaces must be retained on board for 3 years. These) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 526.4 Td (records serve as evidence of compliance with safety standards and provide a historical log) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 511.9 Td (of hazardous area usage.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 482.9 Td (The permit file must include the signed original permit, the atmospheric test results) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 468.4 Td (recorded at the time of issuance, and the attendant's log of communication checks. Any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 453.9 Td (incidents or near-misses associated with an entry must be documented in the vessel's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 439.4 Td (official logbook and referenced in the permit file. Regular audits by the Safety Officer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 424.9 Td (will verify that records are complete, legible, and stored securely for the required) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 410.4 Td (retention period.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 56 28 Td (SMS-11 Enclosed Space Entry \(fictional\) - page 3 of 3) Tj ET
endstream
